.Sh THEMES
The theme is the file
.Ql "_ecstatic\&.wattle"
in the source directory.
It is compiled when the site is built,
so it can be changed without rebuilding
.Nm ,
and it can import files beside it by relative path.
.Pp
The theme must define a function,
.Ql "build" ,
that takes a map of the site and returns a vector of pages.
Each page is a map with
.Ql ":path" ,
the path of the file relative to the destination directory,
and
.Ql ":body" ,
its contents as a string or buffer.
A path cannot be absolute or contain
.Ql "\&.\&." .
If any page is invalid,
no page is written.
.Pp
The pages and the site’s static files are written to a new
directory beside the destination,
.Ql "\&.<name>\&.ecstatic-new" ,
which then replaces the destination.
A failed build leaves the previous site in place.
A page cannot have the path of a static file or of another page.
The destination cannot be the source directory or contain it.
.Pp
The theme can define
.Ql "config" ,
a map that is passed to
.Ql "build"
as
.Ql ":config" .
.Nm
reads these keys from it:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Ql ":offset"
.Xc
The offset from UTC of the site’s dates,
such as
.Ql "\(dq+0900\(dq" .
It applies to dates in URLs and to dates written without an
offset.
This defaults to
.Ql "\(dq+0000\(dq" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":include"
.Xc
A vector of paths beginning with
.Ql "_"
to read,
such as
.Ql "\(lB\(dq_pages\(dq\(rB" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":exclude"
.Xc
A vector of paths to skip,
such as
.Ql "\(lB\(dqGemfile\(dq\(rB" .
.It Xo
.Ql ":future?"
.Xc
Whether to include posts dated in the future.
This defaults to false.
.It Xo
.Ql ":markdown"
.Xc
A map with
.Ql ":options" ,
a vector of cmark options,
and
.Ql ":transforms" ,
a vector of functions.
See
.Sx "MARKDOWN"
below.
.It Xo
.Ql ":keep"
.Xc
A vector of paths in the destination to carry over to the new
site,
such as files that Git tracks.
This defaults to
.Ql "\(lB\(dq\&.git\(dq \(dq\&.gitkeep\(dq \(dq\&.svn\(dq\(rB" .
.El
.Pp
The theme can also define
.Ql "permalink" ,
a function that takes a post and returns its URL.
Without it,
a post’s URL is
.Ql "/<categories>/<yyyy>/<mm>/<dd>/<slug>\&.html" .
A
.Ql "permalink"
in a post’s front matter takes precedence over both.
.
.Sh CONTENT
The source directory is read as Jekyll reads it:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n -compact
.It
A file under
.Ql "_posts"
named
.Ql "YYYY-MM-DD-slug\&.ext"
that begins with front matter is a post.
Subdirectories of
.Ql "_posts"
are read.
.It
Any other file that begins with front matter is a page.
.It
Any other file is static.
.El
.Pp
A file or directory whose name begins with
.Ql "_"
or
.Ql "\&."
is skipped unless it is under a path in
.Ql ":include" .
A post or page whose front matter sets
.Ql "published"
to false is skipped.
.Pp
Front matter is YAML between lines of
.Ql "---" .
Only a subset of YAML is read:
plain,
single-quoted and double-quoted scalars,
flow lists such as
.Ql "\(lBa, b\(rB" ,
nested maps and literal block scalars.
Other syntax is an error.
.Pp
The site map passed to
.Ql "build"
has these keys:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ql ":config" ,
.Ql ":source"
and
.Ql ":destination" .
.It
.Ql ":revision" ,
the commit hash of
.Ql "HEAD"
in the repository containing the source directory,
or nil,
and
.Ql ":time" ,
when the build started.
.It
.Ql ":posts" ,
newest first.
Each post has
.Ql ":path"
(relative to the source directory),
.Ql ":url" ,
.Ql ":slug" ,
.Ql ":date"
(seconds since the epoch),
.Ql ":title" ,
.Ql ":categories" ,
.Ql ":tags" ,
.Ql ":front-matter" ,
.Ql ":content"
(the text after the front matter),
.Ql ":html" ,
.Ql ":excerpt"
and
.Ql ":modified" ,
the time of the last commit to change the file or,
if there is none,
the time the file was modified.
.It
.Ql ":pages" .
Each page has
.Ql ":path" ,
.Ql ":url" ,
.Ql ":title" ,
.Ql ":front-matter" ,
.Ql ":content" ,
.Ql ":html" ,
.Ql ":excerpt"
and
.Ql ":modified" .
A page’s URL is its
.Ql "permalink"
or its path,
with Markdown files ending in
.Ql "\&.html"
and
.Ql "index\&.html"
giving the URL of its directory.
.It
.Ql ":static" ,
the paths of the static files.
.El
.
.Sh MARKDOWN
Posts and pages whose paths end in
.Ql "\&.md" ,
.Ql "\&.markdown" ,
.Ql "\&.mkdown" ,
.Ql "\&.mkdn"
or
.Ql "\&.mkd"
are converted from Markdown with cmark-gfm into
.Ql ":html" .
Other posts and pages have their content as
.Ql ":html" .
The
.Ql ":excerpt"
is the
.Ql "excerpt"
in the front matter or,
for Markdown,
the HTML of the text before the first blank line.
.Pp
The
.Ql ":options"
of the Markdown configuration are keywords for cmark’s options:
.Ql ":footnotes" ,
.Ql ":smart" ,
.Ql ":unsafe" ,
.Ql ":hardbreaks" ,
.Ql ":nobreaks" ,
.Ql ":sourcepos" ,
.Ql ":validate-utf8" ,
.Ql ":github-pre-lang" ,
.Ql ":liberal-html-tag"
and
.Ql ":full-info-string" .
Without
.Ql ":unsafe" ,
raw HTML is left out.
.Pp
Each of the
.Ql ":transforms"
is called with the document node after parsing and before rendering.
It edits the tree with these functions,
which the theme can use without importing anything:
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ql "cmark/nodes" ,
.Ql "cmark/children"
and
.Ql "cmark/parent" ,
which find nodes.
.Ql "cmark/nodes"
returns the node and its descendants in document order,
as they were when it was called.
.It
.Ql "cmark/type" ,
which returns a node’s type as a keyword,
such as
.Ql ":paragraph" ,
.Ql ":text" ,
.Ql ":code-block"
or
.Ql ":footnote-reference" .
.It
.Ql "cmark/literal" ,
.Ql "cmark/fence-info" ,
.Ql "cmark/url" ,
.Ql "cmark/title"
and
.Ql "cmark/heading-level" ,
and the setters
.Ql "cmark/set-literal!" ,
.Ql "cmark/set-fence-info!" ,
.Ql "cmark/set-url!"
and
.Ql "cmark/set-title!" .
.It
.Ql "cmark/new" ,
which makes a node of a type in the same document,
and
.Ql "cmark/insert-before!" ,
.Ql "cmark/insert-after!" ,
.Ql "cmark/append-child!" ,
.Ql "cmark/prepend-child!"
and
.Ql "cmark/unlink!" ,
which move nodes.
.El
.Pp
A theme can also call
.Ql "markdown/render"
and
.Ql "markdown/inline" ,
which renders Markdown without
.Ql "<p>"
tags,
with a Markdown configuration.
.
.Sh HELPERS
A theme can use these functions without importing anything.
Each has a docstring.
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ql "hiccup/html" ,
.Ql "hiccup/html5"
and
.Ql "hiccup/xml"
write Hiccup:
an element is a vector of a tag keyword (with an ID and classes,
as in
.Ql ":div#main\&.post" ) ,
an optional map of attributes and the children.
Text is escaped;
.Ql "hiccup/raw"
marks HTML that is not.
.It
.Ql "date/format"
formats a time at an offset with strftime directives,
such as
.Ql "\(dq%-d %B %Y\(dq" .
.Ql "date/rfc3339"
and
.Ql "date/rfc822"
give the forms feeds use.
.It
.Ql "paginate/pages"
splits items into numbered pages.
.It
.Ql "feed/atom" ,
.Ql "feed/rss"
and
.Ql "feed/json"
write feeds.
.It
.Ql "highlight/load-grammars"
loads the TextMate grammars (\c
.Ql "\&.json"
files)
in a directory into a map of scope names to grammars,
and
.Ql "highlight/lines"
returns the HTML of each line of code highlighted with a grammar.
Each token is a
.Ql "<span>"
with a class such as
.Ql "hl-keyword" ,
.Ql "hl-string"
or
.Ql "hl-comment" .
A Markdown transform can use them to replace code blocks.
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A theme that writes one page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\*(lpdef config {:title \(dqExample\(dq}\*(rp

\*(lpdefn build \(lBsite\(rB
  \(lB{:path \(dqindex\&.html\(dq
    :body \*(lpstring \(dq<h1>\(dq \*(lpget-in site \(lB:config :title\(rB\*(rp \(dq</h1>\(dq\*(rp}\(rB\*(rp
.Ed
.Pp
Build the site in
.Ql "src"
into
.Ql "public" :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cd src
$ ecstatic build
.Ed
.
